        {
          "id": 449996989,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "`H264 Presentation Timestamp` is a time stamp itself which is first 4 bytes of payload.\n\nIn documentation this field referred as `ptv`.\nIt also named `CVF_FIELD_H264_PTV` in [libavtp](https://github.com/Avnu/libavtp/blob/master/include/avtp_cvf.h)\n\nI'd suggest to change it to `H264 PTV` with string description `Is set` and `Is not set` (`tfs_bit_set_not_set`).\n\nIn this case `tfs_marker_bit_set_not_set` also may be replaced with `tfs_bit_set_not_set`",
          "author": {
            "id": 7652695,
            "username": "dima.buzdyk",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dima Buzdyk",
